# Firmware Main Orchestration Contract

## Composition Root

`main.cpp` instantiates all concrete classes and wires them together:

```cpp
int main() {
    Config config = load_device_config();

    domain::Location current_location{};

    GpsReader gps{GpsReader::Config{/* uart params */}};
    WifiManager wifi{WifiManager::Config{/* ssid/password */}};
    ApiClient api{wifi, ApiClient::Config{/* base_url, api_key */}};
    Display display{Display::Config{/* lcd enabled */}};
    BatteryMonitor battery{BatteryMonitor::Config{/* adc pin */}};
    LocalQueue queue{LocalQueue::Config{/* max entries */}};
    Timer fix_timer{Timer::Config{pdMS_TO_TICKS(1000)}}; // 1 Hz

    gps.start();
    display.show_status("Booting");

    while (true) {
        // 1. GPS reads
        if (fix_timer.has_elapsed()) {
            fix_timer.start();
            std::optional<domain::Location> loc = gps.read_location();
            if (loc) {
                current_location = *loc;
                display.show_location(current_location);
            }
        }

        // 2. WiFi + send
        if (wifi.is_connected()) {
            if (current_location.satellites == 0) {
                // GPS timeout fallback
                current_location.is_stale = true;
            }
            bool sent = api.send_location(current_location);
            if (!sent) {
                // handled internally by ApiClient retry/queue logic
            }
        } else {
            wifi.connect();
        }

        // 3. Battery (low priority)
        std::optional<double> volts = battery.read_voltage();
        // update display if needed

        vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(10));
    }
}
```

## Communication Rules
- Synchronous: direct return values
- Asynchronous: not strictly required in Phase 1; event queue can be added in Phase 2

## Error Recovery
- `ApiClient` retries 3 times (1s, 2s, 4s) then sets `is_stale = true` on last-known position.
- `LocalQueue` stores positions when WiFi is down; flushed on reconnection.
